  "issues": [
    "The late_winner failure was caused by exceeding the per-interaction tool call limit (emitting 24 tool calls in a single turn) leading to 'tool_call_limit', not max_steps exhaustion.",
    "Reducing max_steps from 8 to 4 does not resolve tool-call budgeting issues, nor does it provide a >10% token reduction since reference and level_not_body already finish in 2 and 3 iterations respectively.",
    "Retaining observation_chars at 4000 fails to compress prompt tokens for tasks where full 4000-character dumps are placed into message history."
  ],
  "recommendation": "Reject the proposal; changing max_steps from 8 to 4 does not prevent the assistant from hitting the per-step tool call limit demonstrated in late_winner, risks premature termination for legitimate multi-step queries, and fails to achieve the required 10% token savings across the suite."
